{"t": 1794104800.9146533, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_branch", "args": {"branch": "fix/rates-rounding", "from_branch": "main", "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794104802.7722976, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/rates-rounding", "files": [{"content": "def convert(amount_minor: int, rate: float) -> int:\n    return round(amount_minor * rate)\n", "path": "worker/rates.py"}], "message": "Restore rounding in FX conversion\n\nint() truncates, which drops a minor unit when the float product lands\njust below the integer (e.g. 1099.9999999999998 -> 1099). Revert to\nround() so converted totals reconcile.\n\nFixes Sentry issue LEDGER-WORKER-9A (regression from #412).", "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794104810.4302099, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Reverts the `int()` truncation introduced in #412.\n\n`int(amount_minor * rate)` truncates instead of rounding, so a float product that lands just under the next integer (e.g. 1099.9999999999998) loses one minor unit. This is the cause of Sentry issue LEDGER-WORKER-9A (ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit, 2,201 events, first seen in release 2026.11.3).\n\nRestores `round(amount_minor * rate)`, the behaviour prior to #412.\n\nSentry: https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/", "head": "fix/rates-rounding", "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker", "title": "Fix FX conversion rounding regression (LEDGER-WORKER-9A)"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794104813.2544305, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Regression flag: this change is the suspect cause of a production error.\n\nSentry issue **LEDGER-WORKER-9A** \u2014 ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit (expected 1100, got 1099). 2,201 events, first seen in release ledger-worker@2026.11.3; Sentry marks commit 8c2f1d0 (\"Speed up FX conversion\", this PR) as the suspect commit.\n\nCause: replacing `round()` with `int()` truncates instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, so products that land just below the integer lose one minor unit. Fix PR restores `round()`.\n\nError: https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794104815.4163136, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_get_file_contents", "args": {"owner": "acme", "path": "worker/rates.py", "ref": "refs/heads/fix/rates-rounding", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
